        </p>

        <h2 class="heading-lg measure">Setup: what we need from you and how long it takes</h2>
        <p>
          We do not publish a day count for this build. Scope sets the clock.
          A narrow follow-up and a wider lead-to-invoice pipeline are not the
          same job, which is why setup runs $1,500 to $5,000 depending on
          scope. The audit fixes the number before you commit. Nothing sends
          until you sign off.
        </p>
        <p>What we need before the first ask goes out:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>The system the job lives in.</strong> ServiceTitan, Housecall Pro, Jobber, or whatever you already pay for. The job-complete event in that system fires the ask.</li>
          <li><strong>Your definition of done.</strong> Tech left, invoice paid, or customer signed off. We use your line, not a default we picked.</li>
          <li><strong>Who may receive it, and who must not.</strong> The customer the job was for, under rules you write. Not a purchased list. Not every number in the phone.</li>
          <li><strong>The wording, including the way to stop.</strong> You read it. You sign off. Incentivized language does not make the cut, and neither does a gate.</li>
          <li><strong>The assessment, then the audit if you want the map first.</strong> The 15-minute assessment is free. The AI Operations Audit is $999 flat, and that fee credits toward a build started within 60 days.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Questions before that call go through the
          <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
        </p>

